./Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/VPNManagerRepository.swift:275:/// Serialized repository for the one app-owned `NETunnelProviderManager`.
./LOGBOOK.md:10:- VALIDATION: All four profiles have team/prefix `262RZ595FP`, the exact application identifier, platform `OSX`, only the current Mac (`sha256:8ea3983a9990`), current validity through 2027-08-10, and unsuffixed `packet-tunnel-provider` without the Developer ID suffix. `com.apple.security.application-groups` is absent. The profile-only `keychain-access-groups = [262RZ595FP.*]` wildcard is expected under rule K2 and is not a finding.
./LOGBOOK.md:14:### 2314 — Gate P0 Apple-account audit separates portal access from organization eligibility (TASK-260715-apc34w)
./LOGBOOK.md:15:- TECHNICAL EVIDENCE: Ceremony C1 records an authenticated Relux Works, LLC portal/team session and authority for matrix `2026-07-28.r12`. A team-scoped Xcode capability bundle refreshed on 2026-08-10 reports Network Extensions as public and editable for development and Developer ID distribution; local signing inventory includes the Relux Works Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities.
./LOGBOOK.md:17:- DEVICE POLICY: The locally available Mac is recorded only by a truncated SHA-256 reference, model class, OS, and architecture; no full device identifier is persisted. The physical-iPhone row remains the named ADR-024 deferred gap owned by `TASK-260715-1kntdx`, neither pass nor failure and not a macOS Gate P0 blocker.
./LOGBOOK.md:32:- AUTHORITY: The owner confirmed an authenticated Apple Developer session for Relux Works, LLC and authority for revision `2026-07-28.r12`: exactly the four macOS App IDs, Network Extensions on all four, and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered. No App Group record/capability, Keychain access-group portal mutation, iOS App ID, distribution profile, or `works.relux.proxy` change is authorized.
./LOGBOOK.md:241:- DECISION: `com.apple.security.application-groups` is now **prohibited on the iOS probe pair** (verdict 04 F3). r4 granted it because the probe "exercises the same shared-container path production depends on" — but `TASK-260715-1jckn0` scopes the probe to the `NETunnelProviderManager` lifecycle and versioned app messaging, its AC3 puts the whole exchange on `sendProviderMessage`, and no shared container appears anywhere. Rule G4 gained **`probeRule`**: a probe inherits **identifiers and profile classes, never entitlements**; if a probe is meant to prove a capability can be *provisioned*, that is a verification deliverable and must be an acceptance criterion **first** — the entitlement follows the criterion, not the reverse.
./LOGBOOK.md:288:- ROOT CAUSE: The r1 matrix assigned `packet-tunnel-provider-systemextension` to all four macOS targets unconditionally while authorizing **Mac Development** profiles for the same four App IDs. Apple DTS is explicit that the value follows the distribution channel: the `-systemextension` suffix is for direct Developer ID signing, and "otherwise — including when you distribute the app on the App Store and when signing for development — use the values without that suffix" (forums/thread/800887). Ceremony C1 would have provisioned development profiles against a value development signing never uses, and C1 is a one-shot human node (ADR-028).
./LOGBOOK.md:338:- ANOMALY: Round 2 removed `1u2vpc ← 2ayxqn`, which scheduled the libssh2 functional/rekey matrix **before** Gate P0 existed while the matrix scope still required a Gate-P0 provider smoke on this Mac. Restored rather than re-scoped, so no Apple-target row is weakened. Consequence: M0 engine selection (`1gjxer`) correctly lands after P0.
./LOGBOOK.md:352:- FINDING: `TASK-260715-32umrc` (generated-project architecture ADR) is blocked by `2ayxqn` (Gate P0). That is why only 35 tasks precede the ceremony — an ADR-011 gate deliberately kept, not a graph defect. Schedule C1 early and run segment 1 alongside arranging it.
./LOGBOOK.md:362:- DECISION: Ceremony C1 deliberately includes the Gate P0 system-VPN approval click. The disposable probe builds in minutes from profiles created minutes earlier, so it stays one sitting. Hold H2 (real app, different bundle identifier) cannot be folded in and remains the next human boundary after 202 autonomous tasks.
