+## 2026-08-11
+
+### 0410 — Disposable macOS packet-tunnel probe reaches external signing-key blocker (TASK-260715-1r0fxv)
+- IMPLEMENTATION: A separate XcodeGen macOS 14 arm64 project now contains `works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac`, exactly one embedded `works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel` app extension, a v1 JSON request/response contract, privacy-safe lifecycle/status reporting, and save/reload/enable/start/message/stop host paths. The provider installs no network settings, reads no packet flow, forwards no packets, and owns no worker tasks.
+- VALIDATION: XcodeGen generation, plist and shell checks, strict Swift format, four Swift Testing cases, the standalone test bundle, and the complete unsigned host/provider graph pass. Xcode's embedded-binary validator accepts the extension shape. `Package.swift`, existing `Sources/`, root `scripts/`, and release workflows remain untouched.
+- BLOCKER: After restoring the hand-maintained entitlement inputs, automatic signing selects the exact approved provider profile `ef64bcae-00ac-458f-94dc-45834429fe80` and one of its authorized Apple Development identities, then `codesign` returns `errSecInternalComponent`; the entitlement-bearing archive exits 65. The generated signing entitlement contains the exact team, application identifier, and unsuffixed packet-tunnel capability. A profile-scoped preflight independently confirms that installed identities match both approved profiles but their private keys cannot sign unattended. This isolates unavailable login-Keychain private-key access rather than target, entitlement, profile, or source failure.
+- RESUME: Unlock the login Keychain or grant `codesign` access to the approved Apple Development private key without exporting or recording secrets, then run `Probes/macOSPacketTunnelProbe/scripts/build-and-inspect.sh`. The remaining strict gates are the signed archive, exact UUID/signature/entitlement/nested-code inspection, drift self-tests, installation, provider response, and clean-stop observation.
+
